Fixed — the build passes now. The problem was Angular trying to download the Cairo font from Google mid-build; with a flaky/blocked connection to `fonts.googleapis.com` it dies with `socket hang up`.

**What I changed:**
- Downloaded Cairo (variable font, Arabic + Latin subsets) into [public/fonts/](public/fonts) — `cairo-arabic.woff2`, `cairo-latin.woff2`
- Added `@font-face` rules at the top of [styles.scss](src/styles.scss) with proper `unicode-range` splitting
- Removed the Google Fonts `<link>` tags from [index.html](src/index.html)

**Verified:** `npx ng build` exits 0, and both `.woff2` files land in `dist/freebuff-pos/browser/fonts/` — so the GitHub Actions workflow will build cleanly too, with zero network dependency for fonts. Bonus: the deployed site now loads the font locally (faster, works offline).

Note: Font Awesome still loads from cdnjs at runtime — that doesn't affect the build, but say the word if you want that self-hosted too.

